Error [E0217]: A Cell guard cannot be stored in struct field `guard`
  --> tests/ui/cell_guard_storage.jet:2:5
    |
  2 |     guard: CellReadGuard<Int>,
    |     ^^^^^
 Why: A Cell guard is a temporary loan handle; storing it inside another value could keep the loan after its local scope ends
 Fix: Keep the guard in a local name or a tuple, and use `.map(...)` or `.split(...)` for projections
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0217

